// one-literal-union-rep (owner 2026-10-13) — an INLINE string-literal-union value delivered to a
// `string` destination at every position. The source reps as the interned atom, so every delivery
// owes the atom-to-string widening: a position that forgets it prints the interned id, or slots
// an i32 where a string ref is owed (invalid wasm).
//
// NO `type` DECLARATION MAY BE ADDED: the alias spelling is not the one under test. The proof
// concatenates, which only a real string survives.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function pick(n: i32): "red" | "green" {
  if n > 0 { return "green" }
  "red"
}
// @@VALUE@@
pick(1)
// @@TYPE@@
string
// @@TEST@@
v == "green"
// @@HIT@@
print("w=" + v)
// @@MISS@@
print("miss")
// @@WANT@@
w=green
// @@VALUE2@@
pick(0)
// @@TYPE2@@
string
// @@PROOF2@@
print("c=" + v)
// @@WANT2@@
c=red
